&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;Real-World Evidence in Interventional Radiology: Leveraging National Claims Data&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tarub Mabud, MD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Assistant Professor of Radiology&lt;br /&gt;
Vascular and Interventional Radiologist&lt;br /&gt;
Columbia University Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This session examines how national claims data can address questions in interventional radiology that trials and single-institution series leave open, spanning comparative outcomes, long-term treatment durability, utilization trends, referral patterns, policy impact, and healthcare economics. We will discuss how the Mabud Lab is leveraging Columbia&amp;#39;s instance of the MarketScan Research Databases to broaden our understanding of the value of minimally invasive image-guided procedures. We will also address the practicalities and limitations of working with claims data.&lt;/p&gt;
