&lt;p&gt;Discussing prediction markets, digital influence methods, ethics and standards, and election coverage ahead of the 2026 midterms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Tow Center for Digital Journalism is hosting a one day conference to encourage conversations between journalists and researchers as we navigate the ever-changing and chaotic information landscape leading up to the 2026 midterms. Sessions will cover the current state of AI&amp;rsquo;s role in electoral politics, current digital influence methods, the promise and limits of predictive analytics, and the practical standards newsrooms need when the tools shaping information are moving faster than the institutions meant to check them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Registration closes 24 hours before event start.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ai-and-digital-influence-in-elections-tickets-2003030727827?aff=oddtdtcreator" target="_blank"&gt;RSVP on Eventbrite&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Speaker:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Dr.&amp;nbsp;Suriyanarayanan Vaikuntanathan, University of Chicago&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;quot;Assembling and guiding materials far from equilibrium: A theorist&amp;#39;s perspective.&amp;nbsp;&amp;quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Abstract: &lt;/strong&gt;Living systems assemble, reconfigure, and steer their components using energy-consuming, nonequilibrium processes, capabilities that synthetic materials largely lack. In this talk I will offer a theorist&amp;rsquo;s perspective on how driving and dissipation can be used to organize, assemble, and control materials far from equilibrium. I will discuss general principles that connect energy dissipation to the structures and dynamics a nonequilibrium system can access. I will then turn to control: how can such a system be guided using only local, imperfect information, as biological systems must? Together, these ideas point toward a framework for designing adaptable materials that sense, respond to, and learn from their environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
